      "summary": "Cardrona Alpine Resort is open for skiing today, with a cold winter's day on offer and some low cloud around (\"Cloudrona\") expected to clear. Grooming has laid down crisp winter cord, though there are areas of firm, frozen spring snow, and off-piste is very firm with some wind-polished patches; there's been 1 cm of new snow in the past 24 hours, holding the natural base at 112 cm. It's currently -7°C with moderate southwest winds around 18 km/h gusting to 29 km/h, forecast to reach a high of -6°C and a low of -9°C tonight. Kindy Conveyor, Learner Conveyors, McDougall's Chondola, Whitestar Express, Valley View, Captains Express, T-Bar, Soho Express, Willow's Quad and Wells Pipe Platter are all open, all 10 of 10 lifts running; 8 of 10 terrain zones are open, with Arcadia Chutes and Summit on hold. Main Basin and Valley View open from 8:30am, with Captains, Willows and the T-Bar from 9am, and Soho to follow; McPark is closed today ahead of the She'll Be Right event. (Issued: 10:29am, 23 Sep) The access road is chain-free but chains must be carried, with an active road hazard advisory in place. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 10 / 10 Runs Open 0 / 38 Percent open 0 %",
